Z||000003||TRiAD||07-05-2001||10:23 AM||||Cool story...Drag kits are turbo kits, for anyone not versed in Civic mods here. DRAG is actually the company name. IMHO they make the best kits out there for those cars. I still prefer SCs. (superchargers). <BR>I wonder if the Civic was waiting up in the middle of that run, or if he hadn't sorted the kit out yet...Even a Civic EX (the fastest coupe short of the Si) would have smoked a stock GT. The turbo kit (depending on which trim he has) adds 80-120hp. With 125hp to begin with, this means that Civic was pushing 205-245hp. Wait, no exhaust mods, I take that back, you need a 3" exhaust to fully utilize the Turbo, maybe 160hp or so, in reality. Still, 0-60 on an EX is about 8.0sec to begin with, which is faster than I've seen a GT or Formula Fiero rated at (stock) as of yet. <BR>Hmmm...<P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg">  <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I><p>[This message has been edited by TRiAD (edited 07-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||88formula||07-05-2001||11:33 AM||||Road and Track, Motor Trend, Motor week, Cart and Driver, all of these magazines that tested the fiero GT and Formula got 0-60 times ranging from 7.5-8 seconds and the quarter mile times around 15.8-16 seconds. The sixty degree v6 engine responds well to tradition engine modifications and with a good driver 0-60 seconds in 7 seconds and the quarter mile in 15.5 is achievable. There was a discussion a little while back where a forum member here who is into SCCA events gets 0-60 mph in 6.5 seconds with his nearly stock fiero.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Slammed Fiero||07-05-2001||11:48 AM||||It seems people don't listen..<P>George Balzer ..15.2 in a Bone stock 86 GT.<BR>I have pulled 6.5's to sixty with forum members as witnesses<P>A si with a 70hp shot of NOS is still only a high 14 sec car. Thereis a kid here at school that has a Greddy kit on his 94 si , it runs 15's flat.<P>I emailed jackson racing about an SC for my old 88 si last year. They said I could expect low 15's in the 1/4 with thier std kit.<P><BR>Magazines don't really mean much .there good for a baseline but thats about it.<P><BR>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000006||85blackgt||07-05-2001||01:02 PM||||slammed man how do you manage to memorize this stuff? i only wish i could memorize this stuff about different cars!<P>------------------<BR>I stick my head out the window,when its closed instead of air i get glass stuck into my head,the city's sounding i can't seem to stop the pounding, can't keep my thoughts from flying round, not sure  what im thinking about, i got SOUL DOUBT!!!- NOFX<P>1986 Fiero SE 2.8lv6||||reg||6
Z||000007||TRiAD||07-05-2001||03:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 88formula:<BR><B>Road and Track, Motor Trend, Motor week, Cart and Driver, all of these magazines that tested the fiero GT and Formula got 0-60 times ranging from 7.5-8 seconds and the quarter mile times around 15.8-16 seconds. The sixty degree v6 engine responds well to tradition engine modifications and with a good driver 0-60 seconds in 7 seconds and the quarter mile in 15.5 is achievable. There was a discussion a little while back where a forum member here who is into SCCA events gets 0-60 mph in 6.5 seconds with his nearly stock fiero.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sorry 88, but I have a Motor Trend in front of me right now from 03-88 with their test of the '88 GT in it, and it ran 0-60 in 8.72 and the 1/4 mile in 16.44. This is a 5sp. <P>As for magazines not being accurate, that's bull. Now, I do rely on R&T MUCH more than the others (they never tested the '88 GT, only the Formula), but they are all fairly close. <P>If someone's getting 6.5 0-60, it's no where near stock. That's a 2 second decrease in time, and you don't get that from tires and an intake. <P><BR>||||reg||1
