Z||000014||Slammed Fiero||07-06-2001||12:47 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Alex4mula:<BR><B>0-60 in 6.5 on stock Fiero?? Maybe it had a blue printed engine from factory...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Fierolisa was in the car with me when I did it at Norwalk.<P>Chris moore saw the GTEC flashing 6.54 sec.<BR>I have done it on 2 different Gtecs , 4 months appart.<P>Look at my sig below for the mods , not much really in the way of motor mods (ie nothing)<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">       <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals, White face Gauges , 75Hp Shot of NOS Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
Z||000015||TRiAD||07-06-2001||02:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B> Fierolisa was in the car with me when I did it at Norwalk.<P>Chris moore saw the GTEC flashing 6.54 sec.<BR>I have done it on 2 different Gtecs , 4 months appart.<P>Look at my sig below for the mods , not much really in the way of motor mods (ie nothing)<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Slammed, I really don't want this to go where it could be going, but there are a few things worth mentioning here...<BR>1) 0-60 in 6.5 is really quick...Especially with a passenger and those 17" wheels will cost you at least .5 as well. <BR>The car does not look anything near stock, and your sig confirms it. Also, were you running the NOS you have listed when you did it? <BR>One last thing. It's GTECH...as in Tesla Electronics G-TECH Pro. There is always the possibility you calibrated it wrong. You MUST dial it in to "0" in G's mode before you can run the other tests. Most people miss that part. <P>Just my $.02. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000016||Klown||07-07-2001||04:57 PM||||Just for reference, I have the April 1996 issue of High Performance Pontiac magazine where they tested several Pontiacs in their bone stock form to see how they did in the 1/4 mile.  The Fiero they tested was an 87 GT with an automatic transmission and about 53,000 miles on it.  The car was able to run 16.78 sec at 79.09 mph.  Now if someone was able to pull this off with an automatic, would it be reasonable to assume that someone with a manual transmission would be able to cut a full second or more of their 1/4 mile time?  I think it's possible.||||reg||1
Z||000017||banditbalz||07-08-2001||10:50 AM||||I am the one that SlammedFiero refered to as pulling 15.2 at 90mph in my 86 GT. The car is a 4 speed with 170,000 kms on the original stock engine. My 1.9sec 60 foot times would make me "guess" that i am well under 7 seconds to 60 mph. Just last night I ran with a Z06 Corvette and held him until 3rd gear. He started pulling away at that point (about 60 mph). I have a friend that has a fresh engine in his GT with an auto tranny. His engine breathes through a cold air intake, Crane cam and ported exhaust. He runs 1.5 seconds behind me in the quarter mile. I attribute this to the slushbox tranny. This same friend witnessed my encounter with the Vette. All I am saying is, I must have one of those rare "uh humm, blueprinted engines from the factory"<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/biglaunch_2.jpg">   <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/banditbalz/" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/banditbalz/</A> <P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!<BR><p>[This message has been edited by banditbalz (edited 07-08-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000018||Slammed Fiero||07-08-2001||11:53 AM||||for starters, Yes I have 17" wheels , But they are actually the same diameter as the original tires. No I never used the NOS , infact the NOS is still being shipped to me as I type this (It was sent thursday) I have been using a gtec for many years , since they first came out infact. I know how to calibrate it just fine. My first time was at the 97 Michigan show. I was pulling off low 7's , but I attribute this to really short 23" tall tires on a stock setup.<P>Georges car is fast...There's nothing more to say there. Its's just plain fast.<P>My mods are 90%+ Suspension. I have an accel coil , cold air induction, bosch platinums, no cat, no egr , looped coolant lines to the TB. I have 255/40/17 Pirelli P Zero "C" Tires , I got them when my dad bought his 911 and went to 18's. There Pirelli's spec race tire ,  There not available here since the car was imported , performance wise there far better than BFG comp Ta ZR's (I used to run) , Pilots , the bad part is that they wear like an R1 tire. I can launch the car really hard with the suspension setup , no wheel hp.<P>Shaun41178 is running 5.6 to 60 on his NOS , I expect low 5's on the bottle. The gear ratio makes the car absolute stump puller. I take it you haven't ridden in a car with a 4spd. nearly 60mph in 2nd , 98 in 3rd.<P>I don't know the exact size of my tires , but I do know there within .3 of stock sizes. <P>I put little faith in magazines. They quoted the Zr1 vette as being a 4.5 sec to sixty car, Corvette fever did a real world shootout and kept coming up with 5.4-5.2 sec. The Z06 vette came out they said 13.0 , 12.9 , I have seen them run 12.3'-12.4's ...Stock..<P>Don't put so much faith in magazines. Ride in a 4spd fiero then a 5spd ..big difference on the low end<P>JM <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Slammed Fiero (edited 07-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000019||TRiAD||07-08-2001||09:56 PM||||Again, I'm going to try to be as diplomatic as possible...<P>1) There's absolutely no way a stock Fiero ran with a Corvette Z06 from 0-60. The Vette was just playing with you. <P>2) If you're saying not to put much faith in magazines, why are you using another magazine to dispute them? I have found the big 4 (R&T, MT, C&D, Automobile) to be very reliable, R&T particularly. Not all cars are the same, but it's a good close baseline. My GTI VR6 could pull off 0-60 in 6.8, and R&T said 7.2, that's not 2 seconds off. <P>3) 17's vs 15s has NOTHING to do with "aspect ratio" (your overall wheel/tire combo height), it's a matter of weight, and more importantly, where the weight is located. You have much more weight around the outside of your wheel/tire circumfrance than you would with the 15" setup. This acts much more agains your accelleration than the lighter (tire-only) material of the 15" setup. <P>As for the magazines and 0-60 times, it's just a matter of what's printed (for actual times) and common sense (the Z06 BS). The wheel/tire info is well documented on any performance site (check SCCA related sites in particular). <P>I know we all have opinions, but there are just some things that go beyond opinion, and we're all here to find the truth, aren't we?<P>Thanks!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000020||88formula||07-08-2001||10:42 PM||||The poor guy has a time slip man! <P>The problem with using performance data from magazines is the many variables that affect an engines performance at the time of testing. Air temperature, elevation, humidity, driver skill, tire traction, engine condition, and the list goes on all make the results from one party testing a car different from and results of another. I have read many articles on the v6 fiero where they get 0-60 times ranging from 7.5 to 8 seconds. In the GM brochure I have they list an 88 GT as having a 0-60 time of 8.7 seconds.  <P>About the cold air induction, isn't the stock fiero intake system a cold air induction? Why would you purchase a cold air induction if the car already has one? That question is not aimed at anyone by the way. I'm staying neutral on this one.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
